                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "121889474",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198309907946",
                            "num_reviews": 2,
                            "playtime_forever": 383,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 116,
                            "last_played": 1787417698
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Really unique and fun - there is a learning curve, it takes some time to learn how to best control your shapes, but once you start getting the hang of it it's tons of fun. Games are only enjoyable within structures and rules - this game has solid structural physics and limits that challenge and reward you. I've been looking for an \"asteroids\" type game but more evolved and with more depth - and this is it in every way. Would love to see an update with more customizable settings for how arenas look, perhaps with ability to make things less busy visually. But overall super fun!",
